WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.300
A coroner links the 75-year-olds cardiac arrest to CJC-1295 and Ipa Morellin. This is Peptides Weekly,

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:13.820
episode 7, education and evidence, never-dosing advice. After that finding, a U.S. enforcement

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:19.760
change on six unapproved peptides, two company diabetes reports, then compounding copies

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:25.020
and what published checks actually show. Richard Norton was an Australian actor, stuntman,

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:31.180
and fight choreographer. The Guardian reports he went into cardiac arrest in March 2025 after

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:37.900
injecting CJC-1295 and Ipa Morellen that a doctor had prescribed even though they were unapproved.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:44.200
Victorian coroner David Ryan treated that sequence as a coronal finding, not as a clinical trial.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:49.400
He was not satisfied those peptides should stay available for medical practitioners to prescribe.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:55.640
In March 2025, Norton asked practitioner Jersey Muchnicki about peptide therapy.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:01.320
The report says they talk through the experimental nature of the treatment, the risks and the absence

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:04.220
of therapeutic goods administration approved alternatives.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:09.440
Another practitioner had already prescribed peptides for fatigue, shoulder pain, and

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.420
loss of muscle mass.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:13.980
Blood tests checked baseline health and contraindications.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:18.260
Norton signed a consent form that listed anaphylaxis among the risks.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:24.120
The injections were prescribed on the 19th of March. Ryan asked the Therapeutic Goods Administration

00:01:24.120 --> 00:01:29.740
to review benefit and safety. He suggested considering a move from schedule 4, prescription

00:01:29.740 --> 00:01:36.440
only, to schedule 10, limited to clinical trials or other experimental use. His reason was

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:41.960
uncertain therapeutic benefit and safety risks that are not fully known. ABC News frames

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:47.913
the death as possibly the first confirmed fatality tied to unapproved peptides. Health and

00:01:47.913 --> 00:01:51.373
Human Services has now published an enforcement discretion policy.

00:01:51.793 --> 00:01:56.113
A week after compounding rules were still an open question rather than a finished rule.

00:01:56.733 --> 00:02:02.053
The BBC reports that Secretary Robert F. Kennedy Jr. released federal registered plans

00:02:02.053 --> 00:02:06.953
letting compounding pharmacies prepare six peptides the Food and Drug Administration has

00:02:06.953 --> 00:02:07.553
not approved.

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:16.093
Those six are BPC-157, TB-500, KPV, MOT-C, Semmax, and Epitalon.

00:02:16.093 --> 00:02:19.593
This is a regulatory action, not evidence the drug's work.

00:02:20.013 --> 00:02:23.593
The draft came from the Health Secretary's Office, not from the FDA.

00:02:24.113 --> 00:02:27.293
A two-week public comment period follows official publication.

00:02:27.893 --> 00:02:34.013
An FDA advisory panel voted in July to loosen restrictions, and FDA staff recommended against

00:02:34.013 --> 00:02:34.673
that step.

00:02:35.253 --> 00:02:40.493
HHS says it will not pursue state licensed pharmacies, federal facilities, or licensed

00:02:40.493 --> 00:02:45.633
doctors who compound those six if they meet rules on ingredient quality, manufacturing,

00:02:45.633 --> 00:02:50.313
monitoring, safety reporting, labeling, and prescriptions written for an individual patient.

00:02:50.673 --> 00:02:55.973
The policy is temporary while the FDA finishes formal rulemaking on the bulk substance list.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:03:01.273
Compounders must report serious adverse events and quality problems such as contamination.

00:03:01.993 --> 00:03:04.353
Compounded drugs are not FDA-approved.

00:03:04.713 --> 00:03:10.693
Kennedy has called himself a big fan of the drugs and has described using BPC-157 for

00:03:10.693 --> 00:03:14.053
a muscle injury, which is a personal report, not a study.

00:03:14.053 --> 00:03:18.233
The partnership for Safe Medicine said the decision leaves a gray area.

00:03:18.673 --> 00:03:23.273
It said FDA scientists had recommended against the substances because of evidence concerns.

00:03:23.933 --> 00:03:28.653
It also said many newly appointed pharmacy compounding advisory committee members appear

00:03:28.653 --> 00:03:30.173
to have conflicts of interest.

00:03:30.793 --> 00:03:36.673
PSM filed a citizen petition last week urging the FDA to disregard the vote, citing insufficient

00:03:36.673 --> 00:03:41.793
evidence and arguing the committee was constituted in violation of the Federal Advisory Committee

00:03:41.793 --> 00:03:44.133
the Act, and the Ethics and Government Act.

00:03:44.793 --> 00:03:50.113
BBC reporting ads that unregulated injectable peptides are marketed online for unproven

00:03:50.113 --> 00:03:55.513
uses, including to teenagers, and that experts point to missing human trials and unknown

00:03:55.513 --> 00:03:56.533
long-term effects.

00:03:57.630 --> 00:04:02.490
Eli Lilly told Stat its investigational drug Reditrutide was more effective at lowering

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:07.670
blood sugar and cutting weight than novel Nordisk's ozempic in a large diabetes study.

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:13.410
That is a company report of a head-to-head study in people with diabetes, not a peer-reviewed

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:14.750
paper in this week's sources.

00:04:15.450 --> 00:04:17.390
Retitrutide remains investigational.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:21.850
OZMPIC is the FDA-approved semiglutide brand for type 2 diabetes.

00:04:23.053 --> 00:04:29.773
Esclidus, in a PR Newswire announcement, reported a placebo-adjusted HBA-1C reduction of 1.7

00:04:29.773 --> 00:04:32.573
percent at 12 weeks for ASC-30.

00:04:33.033 --> 00:04:37.353
ASC-30 is an investigational oral small molecule GLP-1.

00:04:37.353 --> 00:04:43.233
not a peptide. The setting was a U.S. Phase II study in participants with diabetes, and

00:04:43.233 --> 00:04:48.584
the material here is the company announcement, not an independent journal report. MedScape

00:04:48.584 --> 00:04:53.884
reports that hair loss associated with GLP-1 receptor agonists appeared similar by race.

00:04:54.504 --> 00:04:59.724
That framing is an observational association, not a randomized trial, and it does not

00:04:59.724 --> 00:05:05.324
prove the drugs cause hair loss equally in every group. Also today, a large cohort study

00:05:05.324 --> 00:05:11.244
observational and not randomized, Link tears epitide to a lower short-term risk of endometrial

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:11.744
cancer.

00:05:12.204 --> 00:05:17.684
In male mice, an animal study, and not a human result, Semaglutide showed an early bone

00:05:17.684 --> 00:05:18.464
building signal.

00:05:19.164 --> 00:05:24.044
Medical Republic reports that the peptide-related death has spurred a call for a telehealth inquiry.

00:05:24.544 --> 00:05:30.844
This week's spotlight is compounding, shortages and copies, and a 2025 search of compounding

00:05:30.844 --> 00:05:36.724
websites found 33 semaglutide or terzepatide products whose strength, root, or added ingredients

00:05:36.724 --> 00:05:38.784
differed from FDA-approved versions.

00:05:39.224 --> 00:05:44.204
That map is a product survey in the annals of pharmacotherapy, not a trial of patients.

00:05:44.924 --> 00:05:49.564
Compounding means a pharmacy prepares a medicine instead of dispensing the manufacturer's approved

00:05:49.564 --> 00:05:50.044
product.

00:05:50.664 --> 00:05:54.984
Shortage rules had been the practical opening for semaglutide and terzepatide copies.

00:05:55.684 --> 00:06:00.824
Semaglutide is a glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonist, a peptide that acts as

00:06:00.824 --> 00:06:06.544
that receptor. A narrative review in the American Journal of Managed Care states it is FDA-approved

00:06:06.544 --> 00:06:12.984
as ozemic for type 2 diabetes, and as wagovi for overweight or obesity. Demand, social media

00:06:12.984 --> 00:06:18.804
attention, shortages and costs then drew both legal and illegal compounded versions. Once the

00:06:18.804 --> 00:06:23.904
innovator shortage was resolved, the analyst paper says pharmacies could legally sell only unique

00:06:23.904 --> 00:06:29.564
products, a different route, a different dosing approach, or extra ingredients, not a simple copy.

00:06:29.564 --> 00:06:33.744
The survey ran from February 3rd to March 20th, 2025.

00:06:34.244 --> 00:06:39.264
Two-thirds of the 33 products contained semiglutide and one-third contained tersepotide.

00:06:39.724 --> 00:06:44.964
Forty-eight percent combined one of those drugs with some mix of cyanocabolamine, glycine,

00:06:45.464 --> 00:06:48.244
niacinamide, docusate, or on dancetron.

00:06:48.684 --> 00:06:53.964
Of 17 single ingredient products, 82 percent were sublingual and 18 percent were oral

00:06:53.964 --> 00:06:55.044
disintegrating tablets.

00:06:55.044 --> 00:07:01.464
Only 18% reported a beyond-use date, and 28% reported preferred storage conditions.

00:07:02.004 --> 00:07:06.864
The authors found little justification for adding nutrients or docusate sodium to combination

00:07:06.864 --> 00:07:12.664
subcutaneous products. They saw a rationale for on-dancetron, but not evidence that giving

00:07:12.664 --> 00:07:17.604
it under the skin works for this purpose. They also saw a rationale for sublingual or

00:07:17.604 --> 00:07:22.324
disintegrating tablets without a finding that those forms beat innovator oral tablets.

00:07:22.324 --> 00:07:28.004
Their conclusion is that safety and efficacy of these compounded products are largely unknown.

00:07:28.524 --> 00:07:36.504
A laboratory analysis, not a human study, tested compounded tersepatide mixed with vitamin B12 analogs from US sources.

00:07:37.064 --> 00:07:47.764
Expert opinion on drug safety reports a widespread, previously unidentified impurity formed when tersepatide reacts with certain B12 analogs, present at substantial levels.

00:07:47.764 --> 00:07:52.304
Those combinations had been mass-marketed as comparable to FDA-approved

00:07:52.304 --> 00:07:57.464
terseptide without evaluation of potency or impurity profiles and sold as

00:07:57.464 --> 00:08:02.164
personalized treatments. Clinical effects of that impurity are unknown. The

00:08:02.164 --> 00:08:06.904
chemistry shows a quality defect, not what the defect does in a person. Human

00:08:06.904 --> 00:08:11.284
evidence in these papers is thinner than the marketing. A retrospective study in

00:08:11.284 --> 00:08:16.964
diabetes, obesity, and metabolism followed 94 people, 81 women and 13 men,

00:08:16.964 --> 00:08:23.004
mean age 46.57 years at a commercial wellness studio. They received once

00:08:23.004 --> 00:08:28.544
weekly compounded semagglutide with cyanokobolamine between June 2023 and

00:08:28.544 --> 00:08:36.064
January 2024. After three months average weight loss was 4.11 kilograms or 4.57

00:08:36.064 --> 00:08:43.664
percent. Fat mass fell by 2.67 kilograms and trunk fat by 1.10 kilograms. Lean

00:08:43.664 --> 00:08:49.564
mass fell by 1.43 kilograms and skeletal muscle mass by 0.88 kilograms.

00:08:50.144 --> 00:08:55.204
As a share of total weight, fat mass decreased while the proportions of lean mass and skeletal

00:08:55.204 --> 00:08:56.004
muscle increased.

00:08:56.704 --> 00:09:02.344
That study is observational and uncontrolled, not a randomized comparison with FDA-approved

00:09:02.344 --> 00:09:06.704
semagglutide, and it cannot show the compounded product matches the approved drug.

00:09:07.324 --> 00:09:11.284
Harms appear in a case series in the Journal of the American Pharmacist Association.

00:09:11.284 --> 00:09:16.744
3 adverse event reports reached a regional poison control center after incorrect administration

00:09:16.744 --> 00:09:21.844
of semi-glutide obtained for weight loss from compounding pharmacies and an aesthetic spa.

00:09:22.524 --> 00:09:25.204
2 patients self-administered 10-fold dosing errors.

00:09:25.824 --> 00:09:30.664
All 3 had nausea, vomiting, and abdominal pain, with most symptoms lasting days.

00:09:31.284 --> 00:09:34.444
One also had headache, anorexia, weakness, and fatigue.

00:09:35.064 --> 00:09:38.744
One sought care and responded to an anti-emetic and intravenous fluids.

00:09:38.744 --> 00:09:42.664
One received a vial and syringes with no pharmacist counseling.

00:09:43.284 --> 00:09:46.544
One reported measuring in milliliters and units rather than milligrams.

00:09:47.064 --> 00:09:51.544
The author's note that vials lack the safety features of pre-filled manufactured pens

00:09:51.874 --> 00:09:53.784
and can allow large overdoses.

00:09:54.244 --> 00:09:59.524
The American Journal of Managed Care Review, narrative rather than new patient data, adds

00:09:59.524 --> 00:10:04.884
that marketed compounded semi-glutide may lack historical quality controls and that fraudulent

00:10:04.884 --> 00:10:06.424
batches have appeared worldwide.

00:10:06.424 --> 00:10:12.784
No paper here shows a compounded copy has the potency, impurity profile, or clinical effect

00:10:12.784 --> 00:10:16.044
of ozempic, wagovii, or approved tirsepatide.

00:10:16.624 --> 00:10:21.604
Advantage of those sublingual or disintegrating compounded tablets over approved oral tablets

00:10:21.604 --> 00:10:22.544
are not determined.

00:10:23.104 --> 00:10:28.204
The 94-person weight change is not proof of safety or equivalence, and three poison center

00:10:28.204 --> 00:10:30.684
cases cannot estimate how often errors occur.

00:10:30.684 --> 00:10:36.344
Ozempic and Wagovi remain the FDA-approved semiglutide products for the uses named above.

00:10:36.744 --> 00:10:41.944
The compounded semiglutide and tear-zepetide products in these papers are not FDA-approved.

00:10:42.324 --> 00:10:46.604
After the innovator shortage resolved, only unique products were described as legally

00:10:46.604 --> 00:10:48.544
sellable by compounding pharmacies.

00:10:49.084 --> 00:10:54.744
Unapproved combinations carry purity, contamination, dosing error, and fraud risks that approved

00:10:54.744 --> 00:10:56.024
pens were built to limit.

00:10:56.024 --> 00:11:03.369
One thing worth knowing is that a coroner's finding, not a trial, treated prescribed CJC-1295

00:11:03.369 --> 00:11:08.589
and Ipa Morellen as unapproved drugs with uncertain benefit and incompletely known risk.

00:11:09.109 --> 00:11:14.549
Company reports on redotrutide and on oral ASC-30 are early human signals and diabetes,

00:11:15.189 --> 00:11:16.669
not settled comparative evidence.

00:11:17.289 --> 00:11:22.149
People given compounded semiglutide outside a trial lost weight and also lost some lean

00:11:22.149 --> 00:11:26.849
and muscle mass, an observational pattern rather than a randomized result for an approved

00:11:26.849 --> 00:11:27.189
pen.

00:11:27.869 --> 00:11:32.669
A three-patient case series shows vial and syringe compounded semaglutide can be measured

00:11:32.669 --> 00:11:38.149
wrong, with days of nausea, vomiting, and pain, which is a harm signal and not a rate.

00:11:38.749 --> 00:11:39.789
That's peptides weekly.

00:11:40.469 --> 00:11:42.749
This show is education, not medical advice.

00:11:43.349 --> 00:11:46.069
Talk to your own clinician before acting on anything you heard.

00:11:46.529 --> 00:11:47.749
I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:11:48.169 --> 00:11:48.789
See you next week.

